    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d465">

                <pb facs="0453" n="441" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg441"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/12–2044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-20T17:00:00+03:25">December 20,
                            1944—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 21—2:53 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>939. Foreign Minister Entezam<anchor n="46" xml:id="d465-f1"/> told me today that
                    Millspaugh and Prime Minister Bayat have reached agreement by which Millspaugh
                    will accept repeal of his economic powers and remain to administer financial
                    affairs under authority granted by law of 21 Aban.</p>
                <p>Mossadegh yesterday introduced into Majlis bill to repeal all Millspaugh powers,
                    including those granted by law of 21 Aban and establish <pb facs="0454" n="442"
                        xml:id="pg442"/> committee of 5 men to supervise operations of Ministry of
                    Finance. His attempt to rush this through failed, however, and Majlis has as yet
                    taken no action on it. Entezam expects that Prime Minister’s bill reported in my
                    932, December 15 will be adopted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d465-f1" n="46" xml:id="d465-f1-content">
                <p>Nasrollah Entezam, formerly Minister of Communications, became Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs on December 7, 1944.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
